lighterfs: FUSE over TCP to the host

Under Virtualization.framework the only virtio-fs device is Apple's own
server, so lighter's file server reaches the guest another way: a few TCP
connections to the gateway over the card, each carrying FUSE requests and
replies in the /dev/fuse wire format, with the kernel's FUSE core doing
everything but the transport. Modelled on virtio_fs.c — the same iqueue
ops, the same connection and mount lifecycle — with a socket where the
virtqueue was. Foreground requests are written on the caller's context
without waiting; anything that cannot go at once, and everything sent
from atomic context, goes through a sender thread that owns the socket
until its queue drains. Replies are read straight into the request's
arguments and pages by one thread per connection. Notifications arrive
as replies with `unique` zero and are handed to the FUSE core's
invalidation entry points.

